---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="FAQ | Web Modernization, AI Systems & Public Sector Digital Strategy | Guiding Point Consulting"
  description="Answers to common questions about how Guiding Point Consulting works with public sector prime contractors and nonprofits on website modernization, AI content systems, and human-centered digital strategy."
>
  <!-- Page Header -->
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container hero-content">
      <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <p class="hero-text">Answers to the most common questions about how we work, what we do, and who we serve.</p>
      <p class="hero-subtext">If you do not see your question here, <a href="/contact">reach out directly</a> and we will get back to you quickly.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ Content -->
  <section class="faq-section">
    <div class="container">

      <!-- GovCon Positioning -->
      <div class="faq-category">
        <h2 class="category-title">GovCon Positioning</h2>
        <div class="faq-grid">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Do you work directly with government agencies?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Guiding Point Consulting primarily operates as a subcontractor, partnering with government prime contractors to support the delivery of digital systems, AI workflows, and communication solutions.</p>
              <p>In some cases, we may work directly with mission-driven organizations, but our primary focus is supporting contract delivery through prime partnerships.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Do you replace or compete with prime contractors?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>No. We do not replace or compete with prime contractors.</p>
              <p>We integrate into prime-led teams as a specialized subcontractor, supporting delivery in areas such as website modernization, content workflows, and AI implementation. Our role is to strengthen your delivery, not compete with it.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">How do you work as a subcontractor?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>We plug into existing contract teams to deliver specific components of work that are often underserved or difficult to staff internally.</p>
              <p>This may include website modernization, communication improvements, content workflows, AI implementation, and team training. We align with your scope, timelines, and reporting structure.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">What types of contracts or projects do you support?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>We support contracts that involve public sector digital services, website modernization, communications systems, digital transformation initiatives, and AI adoption.</p>
              <p>Our work is especially valuable in projects where usability, clarity, and long-term sustainability are critical.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Services Clarity -->
      <div class="faq-category">
        <h2 class="category-title">Services Clarity</h2>
        <div class="faq-grid">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Is this just website design or development?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>No. Our work goes far beyond design.</p>
              <p>We modernize websites by improving messaging, structure, usability, and internal workflows while also optimizing for AI-driven discovery through AEO (Answer Engine Optimization) and GEO (Generative Engine Optimization). The result is a website that is not only visually improved, but functional, discoverable, and sustainable for your team.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">What do you mean by "website modernization"?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Website modernization is not just a redesign.</p>
              <p>It involves transforming a website into a clear, usable, and maintainable system that improves communication, supports internal workflows, and aligns with how users and AI tools discover information today. This includes both front-end improvements and back-end systems.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">What are AEO and GEO, and why do they matter?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>AEO (Answer Engine Optimization) and GEO (Generative Engine Optimization) focus on how content is discovered and used by AI tools and modern search systems.</p>
              <p>As more users rely on AI-generated answers instead of traditional search, websites need to be structured in ways that AI can understand and surface. We incorporate these practices to improve visibility, accessibility, and long-term relevance.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Do you provide AI tools or just strategy?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>We provide both strategy and implementation.</p>
              <p>This includes AI-supported workflows, prompt libraries, SOPs, team training, and integration into existing processes. Our focus is on practical systems that teams can actually use.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Process & Engagement -->
      <div class="faq-category">
        <h2 class="category-title">Process and Engagement</h2>
        <div class="faq-grid">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Where do most engagements start?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Most engagements begin with a website and messaging audit.</p>
              <p>This helps identify clarity issues, content gaps, workflow inefficiencies, and opportunities for AI integration. From there, we develop a roadmap and support implementation.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Can you work with our existing team or vendors?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes. We are designed to integrate into existing teams.</p>
              <p>We frequently collaborate with internal staff, developers, designers, communications teams, and prime contractor teams. Our role is to complement, not replace, existing capabilities.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Do you offer ongoing support?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes. We offer ongoing advisory support, fractional digital strategy leadership, and continued optimization of workflows and systems to ensure long-term success after initial implementation.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Digital Transformation -->
      <div class="faq-category">
        <h2 class="category-title">Digital Transformation</h2>
        <div class="faq-grid">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">What is digital transformation, and how do you approach it?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Digital transformation is not just about adopting new tools.</p>
              <p>At Guiding Point Consulting, it means improving how organizations communicate, operate, and deliver their mission through better systems, workflows, and digital experiences. We focus on usability, clarity, and sustainability, ensuring solutions actually work in day-to-day operations.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Fractional Digital Strategy -->
      <div class="faq-category">
        <h2 class="category-title">Fractional Digital Strategy Lead</h2>
        <div class="faq-grid">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">What is a fractional digital strategy lead?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>A fractional digital strategy lead provides senior-level digital guidance on a part-time or contract basis, without the cost of a full-time hire.</p>
              <p>This role helps guide decisions around websites, workflows, AI adoption, and long-term digital strategy.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">When should you consider a fractional digital strategy lead?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>You may need one if:</p>
              <ul>
                <li>You lack in-house digital leadership</li>
                <li>Your team is operating reactively instead of strategically</li>
                <li>You are implementing new systems or tools</li>
                <li>You need experienced guidance without full-time overhead</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">How does a fractional digital strategy lead help?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>A fractional lead helps bring structure, clarity, and direction to your digital efforts. They align systems, reduce inefficiencies, support teams through change, and ensure long-term sustainability, not just short-term fixes.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- AI Team Training -->
      <div class="faq-category">
        <h2 class="category-title">AI Team Training</h2>
        <div class="faq-grid">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Do you provide AI training for teams?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes. We provide practical, hands-on AI training designed for non-technical teams in mission-driven and public sector environments.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">What does AI training include?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Training includes safe AI usage, prompt development, workflow integration, quality control, and governance considerations. We focus on helping teams use AI confidently and consistently.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Why is AI training important right now?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Many teams are already using AI without clear guidelines. This can lead to inconsistent results, confusion, and risk. Training provides structure, clarity, and confidence so AI becomes a reliable tool rather than a source of uncertainty.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Workshops & Speaking -->
      <div class="faq-category">
        <h2 class="category-title">Workshops and Speaking</h2>
        <div class="faq-grid">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Are you available for workshops or speaking engagements?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes. We offer workshops and speaking engagements on AI, digital workflows, website clarity, and communication systems for mission-driven and public sector teams.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Who are these workshops for?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>We work with nonprofits, public sector teams, associations, and leadership groups looking to better understand and apply digital systems and AI.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">What is the goal of these workshops?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Our goal is to provide clear, practical guidance that participants can apply immediately, reducing confusion and improving confidence across the team.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Packages & Structure -->
      <div class="faq-category">
        <h2 class="category-title">Packages and Structure</h2>
        <div class="faq-grid">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Do you offer service packages?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes. We offer structured service packages designed to meet organizations at different stages of need.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">What types of packages do you offer?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Our services typically fall into three levels:</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Foundational — audits and assessments</li>
                <li>Implementation — modernization and systems</li>
                <li>Ongoing Support — strategy and optimization</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Can services be customized?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes. We tailor engagements based on contract requirements, organizational needs, and project scope.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Fit & Qualification -->
      <div class="faq-category">
        <h2 class="category-title">Fit and Qualification</h2>
        <div class="faq-grid">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Who is the best fit for your services?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>We are best suited for government prime contractors and organizations managing complex digital systems who need structured, sustainable solutions.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">Who is not a good fit?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>We may not be the right fit if you are only looking for a basic website design or a quick, low-cost solution without long-term systems or strategy.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Long-Term Value -->
      <div class="faq-category">
        <h2 class="category-title">Long-Term Value</h2>
        <div class="faq-grid">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">How do your services support long-term sustainability?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>We focus on building internal capacity through documented workflows, training, and systems teams can manage. The goal is to reduce dependency and ensure long-term success well beyond the initial engagement.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Bottom CTA -->
  <section class="faq-cta">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="faq-cta-content">
        <h2>Still have questions?</h2>
        <p>Reach out directly and we will get back to you with a straight answer, no sales pitch required.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in Touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  /* ── Page Header ─────────────────────────────── */
  .page-header {
    background: var(--white);
    padding: var(--space-2xl) 0 var(--space-xl);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
  }

  .hero-content {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .hero-text {
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-md);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--gray-600);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .hero-subtext {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--gray-500);
  }

  .hero-subtext a {
    color: var(--rust);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .hero-subtext a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* ── FAQ Section ─────────────────────────────── */
  .faq-section {
    padding: var(--space-3xl) 0;
    background: var(--off-white);
  }

  .faq-section .container {
    max-width: 860px;
  }

  /* ── Category Block ──────────────────────────── */
  .faq-category {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .category-title {
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--indigo);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--rust);
    display: inline-block;
  }

  /* ── FAQ Grid ────────────────────────────────── */
  .faq-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  /* ── Accordion Items ─────────────────────────── */
  .faq-item {
    background: var(--white);
    border: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  }

  .faq-item[open] {
    border-color: var(--rust);
    box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(117, 19, 18, 0.08);
  }

  .faq-question {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--indigo);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    transition: background 0.2s ease;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .faq-question::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }

  .faq-question::after {
    content: '+';
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--rust);
    font-weight: 400;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    transition: transform 0.25s ease;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .faq-item[open] .faq-question::after {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }

  .faq-question:hover {
    background: rgba(117, 19, 18, 0.03);
  }

  .faq-answer {
    padding: 0 var(--space-lg) var(--space-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--gray-100);
  }

  .faq-answer p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--gray-700);
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 0;
  }

  .faq-answer p:first-child {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  .faq-answer ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 0;
  }

  .faq-answer li {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    position: relative;
    color: var(--gray-700);
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .faq-answer li::before {
    content: '→';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--rust);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* ── Bottom CTA ──────────────────────────────── */
  .faq-cta {
    padding: var(--space-3xl) 0;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--indigo) 0%, #01141f 100%);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .faq-cta-content {
    max-width: 560px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .faq-cta-content h2 {
    color: var(--white);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .faq-cta-content p {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  /* ── Buttons ─────────────────────────────────── */
  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.875rem 2rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
    border: 2px solid transparent;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--rust);
    color: var(--white);
  }

  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: #5a0e0d;
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(117, 19, 18, 0.3);
  }

  /* ── Responsive ──────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .faq-question {
      font-size: 0.975rem;
      padding: var(--space-md);
    }

    .faq-answer {
      padding: 0 var(--space-md) var(--space-md);
    }
  }
</style>